<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>Each agency, after July 1, 1978, shall inform any person or agency to whom a record containing personal information has been disclosed during the preceding three years of any correction of an error or notation of dispute made pursuant to Sections 1798.35 and 1798.36 if (1)<span class="EnSpace"/>an accounting of the disclosure is required by Section 1798.25 or 1798.26, and the accounting has not been destroyed pursuant to Section 1798.27, or (2)<span class="EnSpace"/>the information provides the name of the person or agency to whom the disclosure was made, or (3)<span class="EnSpace"/>the person who is the subject of the disclosed record provides
  the name of the person or agency to whom the information was disclosed.</p></caml:Content>